.TH WINPE_TERMINAL 8 "2026-11-01" "winpe-terminal 1.0.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
winpe_terminal \- run Windows PE in QEMU/KVM and use it from this terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B winpe_terminal
.I start
.RB [ \-/dev/partition ]
.br
.B winpe_terminal
.BR prepare " [" \-\-force ]
.br
.B winpe_terminal
.BR setting | reload | \-help
.br
.B sudo winpe_terminal
.B \-status
.br
.B sudo winpe_terminal
.BR terminate | stop | shutdown | end | exit
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-x=UUID ]
.br
.B sudo winpe_terminal
.B \-unistall
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B winpe_terminal
starts a Windows PE virtual machine with QEMU/KVM and connects its native
Emergency Management Services console to the calling terminal, so Windows
commands such as \fBchkdsk\fP can be run without rebooting the machine.
.PP
Windows PE is not part of the package. Run
.B sudo winpe_terminal prepare
once to fetch the official Microsoft components after accepting Microsoft's
licence, and to build the image locally.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Start one instance and attach this terminal to it. The terminal and the
instance are one-to-one: closing the terminal stops its instance.
.TP
.BI start " \-/dev/partition"
Additionally expose one whitelisted, unmounted partition to the guest as a
synthetic MBR disk. The device path is given as a single argument with a
leading dash.
.TP
.B prepare
Download, verify and build the WinPE image. Interrupted downloads resume on
the next run.
.TP
.B setting
Show or edit the configuration in \fI/etc/winpe-terminal/config.json\fP.
Saving as a normal user asks for graphical authorisation.
.TP
.B reload
Re-read and validate the configuration. Only later starts are affected.
.TP
.B \-status
Report running instances with their UUID, uptime, PIDs, memory, CPU and the
device that was attached.
.TP
.B terminate, stop, shutdown, end, exit
Ask every running instance to shut down. With
.B \-f
the shutdown is forced, which can lose unwritten data. With
.BI \-x= UUID
only that instance is targeted.
.TP
.B \-unistall
Stop running instances and hand the removal to
.BR "apt-get purge winpe-terminal" .
The spelling is intentional.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/winpe-terminal/config.json
Configuration file managed as a dpkg conffile.
.TP
.I /var/lib/winpe-terminal/
State: the prepared image, build receipt and instance records.
.TP
.I /var/cache/winpe-terminal/
Download cache and build scratch space; safe to delete.
.TP
.I /var/log/winpe-terminal/
One log per instance, named after the instance UUID.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qemu-system-x86_64 (1),
.BR chkdsk .
.PP
